---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
---

<GuidePage
  title="How to Calculate Fabric for Quilt Pieces"
  guideSlug="how-to-calculate-quilt-fabric"
  guideCategory="reference"
  description="Convert finished or cut dimensions into repeated-piece yardage, then combine all project cuts by fabric for a practical plan."
>
  <section>
    <h2>Start with cut dimensions</h2><p>
      Finished dimensions need seam allowance on both opposite edges; cut
      dimensions already include it. Keep quantity, direction, and any WOF-strip
      requirement with each piece.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Use usable width</h2><p>
      Count how many pieces fit across fabric after selvages, then round rows
      upward. Apply purchase safety after the layout and round the purchase
      upward to the shop increment.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Combine a real project</h2><p>
      The <a href="/calculators/fabric-yardage/">fabric yardage calculator</a> handles
      one repeated rectangle. For multiple sizes and stock on hand, use the <a
        href="/fabric-cutting-planner/">project fabric planner</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</GuidePage>
